  "notes": "Official 2024 BCCC program flyer (\"RESPIRATORY CARE, AAS — 64 credit hours — CAREER SUGGESTED SEQUENCE OF COURSES\"). Flyer lists a PROGRAM PREREQUISITES phase (15 credits) plus the sequenced plan (49 credits); both are included and the total reconciles to the flyer's printed 64. 0-credit Computer Literacy Exam and Biology Placement Exam (test out of BIO 101) are documented here only, not in external_prereqs. Accredited by the Commission on Accreditation for Respiratory Care (CoARC). Graduates are eligible to sit for all National Board for Respiratory Care credentialing examinations. Admission is selective (~13-15 students/year, ranked by cumulative college GPA; min 2.5; ENG 101 with C or better). BCCC's 2025-2026 catalog program pages were unreachable via research tools (Academic Programs index requires JS; search/sitemap endpoints 403), so 2024-2025 remains the latest machine-readable official catalog. [Coordinator correction 2026-10-01: total_credits set to 49 (= sum of sequenced course credits) per corpus convention (external_prereqs excluded from the sum; cf. ABAC plans); collector had recorded 64 including the prerequisite phase. The catalog's printed program total and the prerequisite phase remain documented above.]",
